<h2>Measuring your SMS ROI</h2>

<p>Tracking SMS performance is simpler than most channels because the actions are direct and measurable. Focus on these metrics.</p>

<p><strong>Delivery rate.</strong> The percentage of messages that actually reach the recipient. This should be above 95%. If it is lower, you likely have outdated phone numbers in your database that need cleaning.</p>

<p><strong>Response rate.</strong> How many people reply to or click a link in your SMS. For appointment confirmations, you should expect 40% to 60%. For promotional messages, 10% to 20% is strong.</p>

<p><strong>Opt-out rate.</strong> Track how many people unsubscribe after each campaign. A spike means something went wrong. Either the message was not relevant, the timing was off, or you are sending too frequently. Keep this below 2% per campaign.</p>

<p><strong>Conversion rate.</strong> Of the people who clicked or responded, how many took the action you wanted? Booked an appointment, left a review, redeemed an offer. This is the number that connects your SMS efforts to actual revenue.</p>

<p>SMS marketing for small business works because it meets people where they already are: on their phones, ready to act. Respect the channel, keep your messages useful, stay compliant, and you will build a communication tool that consistently drives results.</p>

